<article class="env-lemma" id="039J">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/039J">Lemma <span data-tag="039J">41.3.6</span>.</a> Let $Y$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be locally of finite type. Let $x \in X$. The morphism $f$ is unramified at $x$ in the sense of Definition <a href="/tag/024N" data-tag="024N">41.3.5</a> if and only if it is unramified in the sense of Morphisms, Definition <a href="/tag/02G4" data-tag="02G4">29.36.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/039G" data-tag="039G">41.3.2</a> and the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>